I've implemented the node, but I left out both operations requests. This node's only capability is `wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0`, and the target has no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem to write `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and no HTTP client to reach `metadata.internal.example`. Adding either would mean importing an interface the node isn't granted, and the host would refuse the component. If operations needs input logging or enrichment, it should be added to the graph as its own node or capability (for example a `notifier`/`state-rw` sink or an `http-client` scoped to the metadata host), not hidden inside `StartRun`.

